<BrandGuide
  brandKey="lululemon"
  brand="Lululemon"
  title="Lululemon Size Chart & Fit Guide: Does It Run Small?"
  description="Lululemon runs true to size with intentional compression — leggings feel snug by design, so don't size up. Numeric sizing explained, fit notes, and FAQ."
  fitSections={fitSections}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={related}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>Lululemon runs true to size — the snugness is the point.</strong> Leggings are
    compression fit, so they're meant to feel firm at your true number in the brand's 0–20
    numeric range. Sizing up loses the hold they're engineered for. Expect Align to feel softer
    and less compressive than Wunder Train at the identical size.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>Trust the squeeze:</strong> compression leggings should feel firm on first wear — if they pull on with zero effort, try the number below.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick the line by feel:</strong> Align for soft, low-compression comfort; Wunder Train for locked-in support — same size, different sensation.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the fit label:</strong> product pages state whether a style is fitted, relaxed, or oversized — that designation shifts the fit more than a size step.</li>
    <li><strong>Size jackets for layers:</strong> sculpted styles like the Define are cut close, so go up one if you'll regularly wear them over more than a tank.</li>
  </Fragment>
</BrandGuide>
